.TH "PKGEXEC_RESULT" "3" "" "libpkgexec" "Version 2.2.0"
.SH NAME
pkgexec_result \- sealed native execution evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]#include <libpkgexec/result.h>\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]execution_result\f[R] distinguishes a request rejected before process start from a started process outcome.
Successful evidence requires exact interpreter identity, every requested guarantee, complete requested stream evidence, zero exit status, and verified cleanup.
.PP
Failed evidence retains a typed failure kind, process termination where a process started, guarantees actually established, stream evidence where available, and cleanup outcome.
Every established guarantee must belong to the sealed request; a backend profile may advertise additional capabilities, but an individual result may not claim a different execution policy.
Cancellation before start has no process termination.
Cancellation after start retains cancelled termination.
Both require a matching token whose signal was requested.
.PP
Limit evidence additionally remains exact by kind.
Applying an undeclared limit changes the execution contract and is not admitted as a stronger result.
Resource\-limit failure evidence names the exact requested kind, and both the aggregate and matching kind\-specific guarantees must have been established.
Ordinary nonzero exits, signals, or syscall failures do not become resource\-limit evidence by guess.
.PP
Diagnostic text is retained but excluded from semantic execution identity.
Process IDs, temporary host paths, wall\-clock timestamps, and elapsed time are not execution identity material.
